00:04:08.811 --> 00:04:11.291
- [Voiceover] Lachlan
asks, "I'm new to Medium,

00:04:11.291 --> 00:04:12.791
"how do I build a community on it?

00:04:12.791 --> 00:04:15.731
"Jab, jab, jab, and
hopefully someone notices?

00:04:15.731 --> 00:04:16.891
"Cheers bro."

00:04:16.891 --> 00:04:18.111
- Uh, cheers bro.

00:04:18.111 --> 00:04:19.870
I think the great thing
about Medium and one of the

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:21.611
reasons I invested in it,
one of the reasons we write

00:04:21.611 --> 00:04:24.771
for it is you actually just
have to put out good content

00:04:24.771 --> 00:04:27.151
because they're doing two
things that are intriguing.

00:04:27.151 --> 00:04:28.571
One, there's a viral loop.

00:04:28.571 --> 00:04:30.491
People sharing, recommending
it at the bottom.

00:04:30.491 --> 00:04:33.031
I was one of the early people 
to growth hack a little bit

00:04:33.031 --> 00:04:35.931
and ask for the hit the
recommend which created virality.

00:04:35.931 --> 00:04:39.631
But they also use human editors
who just see a good piece

00:04:39.631 --> 00:04:41.891
of content and populate it to the email,

00:04:41.891 --> 00:04:42.971
to the top of the page.

00:04:42.971 --> 00:04:44.751
This is an incredible
opportunity, my friends.

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:48.111
Medium, in a lot of ways,
has Reddit and Digg dynamics

00:04:48.111 --> 00:04:51.451
that we haven't seen in a
long team where you could be

00:04:51.451 --> 00:04:54.471
anybody, you don't have to
just ooze the juice of your

00:04:54.471 --> 00:04:56.771
social networks to get people
there, but you could be

00:04:56.771 --> 00:04:59.411
anybody who writes a good,
solid piece of content

00:04:59.411 --> 00:05:02.371
and then the machine, not
the community, humans,

00:05:02.371 --> 00:05:05.391
can decide to populate it and
then give you an opportunity

00:05:05.391 --> 00:05:06.291
to then siphon.

00:05:06.291 --> 00:05:08.171
The really Holy Grail for a lot of you,

00:05:08.171 --> 00:05:10.031
and the reason I'm pushing
so many of you in the Vayner

00:05:10.031 --> 00:05:12.011
Nation to write on it is you
can write a nice piece of

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:16.371
content, get lucky, but
probably not lucky 'cause it was

00:05:16.371 --> 00:05:18.271
a good piece of content, but a
little serendipity along with

00:05:18.271 --> 00:05:20.771
that good piece of content
and now you're populated.

00:05:20.771 --> 00:05:23.411
You get, you know, a couple
hundred, a couple thousand,

00:05:23.411 --> 00:05:26.251
people follow you off of the
base of that being featured

00:05:26.251 --> 00:05:27.751
and away you go, you start building.

00:05:27.751 --> 00:05:29.931
And so, that's for
people with no audience.

00:05:29.931 --> 00:05:31.771
For all of you that are lucky
enough to have some Facebook,

00:05:31.771 --> 00:05:34.531
some Twitter, some Instagram
followers and users,

00:05:34.531 --> 00:05:37.451
you should put out content
there and use that as an

00:05:37.451 --> 00:05:38.997
opportunity to be discovered.

00:05:38.997 --> 00:05:43.157
And so, you know, I've used
Facebook very successfully

00:05:43.157 --> 00:05:44.656
to drive people towards Medium.

00:05:44.656 --> 00:05:47.117
Email services to drive
people towards Medium.

00:05:47.117 --> 00:05:48.696
Which then gets people
reading and recommending which

00:05:48.696 --> 00:05:50.897
creates more virality, which
gets more people to recognize

00:05:50.897 --> 00:05:53.157
me and it just becomes this viral loop.

00:05:53.157 --> 00:05:55.397
So it's not about jab,
jab, jab, right hooking,

00:05:55.397 --> 00:05:58.157
where that's a world of put
out content and then ask

00:05:58.157 --> 00:05:59.597
for something.

00:05:59.597 --> 00:06:02.477
This is more about just putting
out good content and letting

00:06:02.477 --> 00:06:04.057
the chips fall where they may.

00:06:04.057 --> 00:06:07.037
I think the other thing you
can do is go out to other

00:06:07.037 --> 00:06:09.937
people that have audiences or
other publications that may,

00:06:09.937 --> 00:06:11.917
then, want to re-publish your publication,

00:06:11.917 --> 00:06:13.957
but has a link that says,
"This was originally written

00:06:13.957 --> 00:06:15.697
"in Medium," and that links.

00:06:15.697 --> 00:06:17.777
And so, you're trying to
create a viral loop because the

00:06:17.777 --> 00:06:20.657
recommend at the bottom
of Medium creates virality

00:06:20.657 --> 00:06:23.073
within Medium, there's a big
audience there and that's

00:06:23.073 --> 00:06:24.687
where your opportunity lies.

00:06:26.047 --> 00:06:28.627
Very tactical off the
gate on a Monday morning.

00:06:29.727 --> 00:06:31.947
- [Voiceover] Stephen asks,
"How do I create value in the

00:06:31.947 --> 00:06:34.107
"services I provide for
clients in the same market

00:06:34.107 --> 00:06:36.128
"while respecting their
competitive advantage?"

00:06:37.017 --> 00:06:37.998
- That's interesting.

00:06:37.998 --> 00:06:40.238
And we kind of play with that
a little bit with VaynerMedia.

00:06:40.238 --> 00:06:41.738
Not that we have any direct competitors,

00:06:41.738 --> 00:06:43.638
but sometimes they're some nuances.

00:06:43.638 --> 00:06:48.038
Providing value to different
companies or individuals

00:06:48.038 --> 00:06:51.358
that are competing in the
same environment is tricky.

00:06:51.358 --> 00:06:53.458
First of all, you know, I
would never be in environment

00:06:53.458 --> 00:06:57.138
of like, Pepsi and Coke,
or where there's complete

00:06:57.138 --> 00:06:59.558
direct competitors, you've
got to be very, very careful.

00:06:59.558 --> 00:07:03.978
Number two, I think
that you need to really,

00:07:03.978 --> 00:07:07.518
really give thought about
how many different thesis'

00:07:07.518 --> 00:07:10.418
and strategies do you actually have?

00:07:10.418 --> 00:07:12.458
How many different things can people do?

00:07:12.458 --> 00:07:14.378
This is where you cannot
just put one, kind of,

00:07:14.378 --> 00:07:17.338
blue print and deploy
it against each client,

00:07:17.338 --> 00:07:19.338
you've got to come up with
unique value propositions

00:07:19.338 --> 00:07:22.058
creatively and strategically,
that allow them to kind of

00:07:22.058 --> 00:07:24.098
offset the competitive set.

00:07:24.098 --> 00:07:27.498
I think the answer is very carefully.

00:07:27.498 --> 00:07:30.858
I think this is a massive
challenge and I think that one

00:07:30.858 --> 00:07:32.558
of the things that I would
recommend to you is actually

00:07:32.558 --> 00:07:37.058
broaden the industries your
in just for that reason.

00:07:37.058 --> 00:07:39.778
Because I think that humans
are emotional and they

00:07:39.778 --> 00:07:41.878
may not, even if you think
that you're proving them

00:07:41.878 --> 00:07:44.838
separate value, they may not.

00:07:44.838 --> 00:07:46.998
And the consumer's perception is king.

00:07:46.998 --> 00:07:50.837
But I think, to me, it's not that hard.

00:07:50.837 --> 00:07:52.618
Because I do think you can
get very different strategies,

00:07:52.618 --> 00:07:55.638
very different creative executions
amongst those strategies

00:07:55.638 --> 00:07:59.257
to make an action that those
companies or individuals

00:07:59.257 --> 00:08:00.558
